### Data Table

```{r}
#| title: "Full Data Comparison"
# Create a formatted table
library(knitr)
table_data <- tuition_data[, c("institution", "tuition", "rank")]
table_data$institution <- gsub("\\.", " ", table_data$institution)
table_data$tuition <- paste0("$", format(table_data$tuition, big.mark=","))
colnames(table_data) <- c("Institution", "Tuition & Fees (2024-25)", "Rank")

# Highlight DePaul row
table_data$Institution[tuition_data$is_depaul] <- 
  paste0("**", table_data$Institution[tuition_data$is_depaul], "**")

kable(table_data, row.names = FALSE, align = c("l", "r", "c"))
```

# Insights

## Row

### Key Findings {width="50%"}

**DePaul's Competitive Position**

-   DePaul ranks **{r} depaul_rank** out of **{r} nrow(tuition_data)** peer institutions
-   Tuition is **{r} format(abs(depaul_tuition - median_tuition), big.mark=",")** ({r} round(abs(pct_diff), 1)%}) **{r} ifelse(pct_diff < 0, "below", "above")** the median
-   Positioned in the **{r} depaul_percentile**th percentile

**Peer Landscape**

-   Median tuition: **\${r} format(median_tuition, big.mark=",")**
-   Range: **\${r} format(min_tuition, big.mark=",")** to **\${r} format(max_tuition, big.mark=",")**
-   DePaul offers a **value proposition** relative to many peers

### Statistical Summary {width="50%"}

```{r}
#| title: "Tuition Statistics Summary"
summary_df <- data.frame(
  Metric = c("Minimum", "1st Quartile", "Median", "Mean", "3rd Quartile", "Maximum", "DePaul"),
  Value = c(
    paste0("$", format(min_tuition, big.mark=",")),
    paste0("$", format(q1_tuition, big.mark=",")),
    paste0("$", format(median_tuition, big.mark=",")),
    paste0("$", format(round(mean(tuition_data$tuition)), big.mark=",")),
    paste0("$", format(q3_tuition, big.mark=",")),
    paste0("$", format(max_tuition, big.mark=",")),
    paste0("$", format(depaul_tuition, big.mark=","))
  )
)

kable(summary_df, row.names = FALSE, align = c("l", "r"))
```

